    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Calculator\n\nA pixel-style two-number calculator built with plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Works offline, no packages, no storage, no network requests.\n\n## Features\n\n- Two numeric inputs: **Left number** and **Right number** (IDs `left` and `right`).\n- Operation selector (ID `operation`) with `add`, `subtract`, `multiply`, `divide`.\n- Calculate button (ID `calculate`).\n- Result output (ID `result`) starts at `0` and shows only the numeric result.\n- Rejects empty or non-finite inputs and division by zero with the exact text `Error`.\n- Supports negative inputs.\n- Keyboard accessible: all controls are labeled and focusable; pressing Enter in either input triggers calculation.\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Open `index.html` in any modern browser.\n2. Enter two numbers (negative values allowed).\n3. Choose an operation.\n4. Click **Calculate** or press Enter.\n5. The result appears below the button.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Offline only; no external assets, imports, or server code.\n- All IDs, labels, and behavior match the specification.\n- Under 200 lines total.\n\n## Files\n\n- `index.html` — complete app (HTML, CSS, JS inline).\n- `README.md` — this file.\n",
      "description": ""
